# iron-plan output. Task-by-task implementation plans, routinely 500-2000+
# lines and per-session. The durable design record is docs/iron/specs/, which
# stays tracked; plans are execution scaffolding and would bloat every diff
# they appear in.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly because it is a data-loss trap: a plan written
# after this rule landed is never committed, so it exists only in the working
# tree that produced it. `git clean -xfd` deletes it, a fresh clone does not
# have it, and iron-build mid-plan has nothing left to execute. Plans are NOT
# "retrievable from git history" -- only the five that predate this rule are.
# If a plan needs to survive, persist it outside the tree (an ironmem drawer;
# see skills/iron-plan/SKILL.md) before cleaning.
docs/iron/plans/

